++  diagnostic:linux-disconnect-container:
++    desc: 'Run the seven k6 HTTP and client controls in one fresh container of the pinned k5 image, into a new OUT directory. Each case serves the unchanged Linux agent and starts a fork/wait payload with guest timeout 20 s. After 2 s it keeps, closes, resets or half-closes the original connection, or gives health a 5 s host deadline. Then it sends health, an ordinary exec and a partial-file download. The threaded case is an experimental control. OUT-outer keeps the identities and the check'
